[semantic-contract] Semantic contract (reviewing)
Files:
spec/initial.md (read-only source)
proposals/semantic-contract.md
crates/engine-core/src/lib.rs
Do:
Translate the vocabulary, pure-function equations, and invariants into typed Rust-facing contracts for LogicalTime, Tau, Context, Journal, Worldline, GameState, Playback, Frame, and Animation.
Define ownership and mutation boundaries so evaluation and presentation cannot mutate authoritative inputs.
Make each unresolved choice below a review gate before downstream implementation begins.
Accept:
The contract preserves distinct LogicalTime and Tau types, state-owned logical time, continuous logical time, immutable worldlines, and render inputs limited to GameState plus Tau.
Each gate has a user-reviewed resolution or an explicit deferred status, and no later task requires an unstated semantic default.
The contract has executable conformance checks for pure evaluation, pure presentation, and reconstructible animation.
Dependencies: none
> Gate: Choose the representation, arithmetic, precision, and range policy for continuous LogicalTime.
> Ruling: Include an event at the evaluation target and apply equal-time events in journal append order.
> Ruling: Temporal definitions are direct indexed lookups at `t_`, not interval mutation from a previous state.
> Ruling: Exact deterministic equality is required; no approximate equality is part of the authoritative model.
> Ruling: Context identity/versioning is deferred unless persistence, compatibility, or networking requires it.
> Gate: Define the closed temporal DSL/index representation and typed out-of-domain results.
> Note: Compiler-checked purity enforcement is deferred to the late purity-hardening stage; early stages record behavioral limitations and executable evidence.
> Gate: Define journal horizon, append, prefix, fork, and invalid-input rules at the contract level.
> Gate: Review the minimum domain-neutral reference fixture before kernel implementation begins.
@guidance text/markdown spec/initial.md
@artifact text/markdown proposals/semantic-contract.md
