[deterministic-kernel] Deterministic state kernel (reviewing)
-> semantic-contract
Files:
crates/engine-core/src/lib.rs
crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
Do:
Implement the reference state(worldline, logical_time) evaluator against the approved contract without owning journal construction or presentation behavior.
Exercise one time-indexed definition and one timestamped authoritative journal fact, including lookup on both sides of the event boundary.
Keep evaluation read-only and make identical immutable inputs produce the same complete GameState.
Accept:
Repeated evaluation of the same worldline and LogicalTime is equal and includes that LogicalTime in the state.
The reference trace demonstrates continuous logical time, event-driven discontinuity, direct indexed lookup, no input mutation, and distinct states for distinct LogicalTime values.
The reference evaluator is the comparison oracle for later optimized implementations.
@artifact text/rust crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
> Gate: Use only the time arithmetic, boundary semantics, event ordering, and reference fixture approved by semantic-contract; this task must not choose them locally.
---
[journal-worldline] Journal and immutable worldlines (reviewing)
-> semantic-contract
-> deterministic-kernel
Files:
crates/engine-core/src/lib.rs
crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
Do:
Implement validated append-only journals, horizon tracking, immutable Context plus journal branches, prefix extraction, and fork construction.
Keep branch creation and event storage separate from state evaluation, and prove parent and child inputs cannot be mutated through either API.
Expose the approved shared-time ordering, journal-owned timestamp assignment, and corrected-branch behavior to the kernel tests without adding merge or networking semantics.
Accept:
Valid append, prefix, and fork operations produce immutable values; invalid timestamps, contexts, and event sequences fail explicitly under the approved contract.
Tests cover equal-time ordering, horizon behavior, prefix agreement before fork, post-fork divergence, parent/child isolation, and unchanged actual journals.
An evaluated branch can be replayed by the deterministic kernel without hidden mutable state.
@artifact text/rust crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
> Ruling: Normal journal writing owns timestamp assignment through a monotonic time cursor; late facts create an explicit corrected branch from a prefix and never mutate the actual journal.
> Gate: Define the journal-writer and corrected-branch construction API; networking, reconciliation, and merge remain out of scope.
> Gate: Resolve branch identity and Context compatibility rules; do not assume merge or network synchronization.
