Do:
Implement pure playback(Tau) -> LogicalTime and the present composition from a Worldline, Playback, and Tau.
Define a renderer boundary that receives only the selected GameState and Tau; keep the core independent of a graphics API.
Test scrub, reverse, past selection, and future selection through the approved playback mapping, with animation reconstructed from immutable definitions and Tau rather than frame history.
Accept:
For fixed inputs, playback, render, animation, and present are deterministic and side-effect free.
The presentation tests prove that no renderer path mutates Context, Journal, Worldline, or GameState and that a future or past selection uses the same state path.
The first visual demo can be hosted without making a graphics framework part of the engine contract.
