[lookahead-counterfactuals] Lookahead and counterfactual histories (reviewing)
-> semantic-contract
-> deterministic-kernel
-> journal-worldline
Files:
crates/engine-core/src/lookahead.rs
crates/engine-core/src/counterfactual.rs
crates/engine-core/tests/lookahead_counterfactual.rs
crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
Do:
Evaluate future state as the same direct indexed query against the current Worldline with its Journal fixed; no unrecorded future event is introduced.
Construct immutable counterfactual forks from a fork time using the approved journal prefix and alternate events, then expose them through the same worldline interface.
Verify that later parent events cannot alter an existing lookahead result or counterfactual and that both actual and alternate branches remain replayable.
Accept:
Future evaluation is exactly state(actual_worldline, future_t) under the approved horizon semantics and records no unrecorded future action.
Counterfactuals agree with their parent before fork_t, can diverge afterward, preserve the actual journal, and remain independently evaluable and presentable.
Tests cover fork boundaries, alternate event validation, fixed-journal lookahead, branch isolation, and playback over either worldline.
@artifact text/rust crates/engine-core/tests/lookahead_counterfactual.rs
@artifact text/rust crates/reference-demo/src/main.rs
> Gate: Define how indexed temporal definitions answer beyond the journal horizon and identify which future inputs are legal for a counterfactual.
> Gate: Define fork-time boundary semantics and alternate-event validation without assuming a merge policy.
