-> lookahead-counterfactuals
Files:
crates/caravan/src/rules.rs
crates/caravan/src/content.rs
crates/caravan/tests/canonical_trace.rs
crates/caravan/assets/
Do:
Choose and implement the smallest recognizable Caravan of Seasons slice as a client of the generic contracts.
Exercise one continuous indexed quantity, one authoritative player event, playback over actual history, fixed-worldline lookahead, and one meaningful counterfactual choice from input through presentation.
Keep game rules, content, input, and assets in the slice; add no game-specific exception to the domain-neutral core.
Accept:
A short fixed trace is deterministic on the reference evaluator and produces the same visible outcomes when scrubbed, projected into the future, or forked counterfactually.
The trace reaches input, journal event, worldline evaluation, playback, and rendered frame in a repeatable playable demo.
The slice is recognizable as the first game loop and any insufficiency in the generic contracts is recorded as a concrete contract gap.
> Gate: The user chooses the canonical slice, minimum playable loop, and first meaningful alternate choice; this task must not invent final game content.
> Gate: Choose the minimum input, asset, and presentation set only within the approved renderer and playback contracts.
