Do:
Define versioned serialization for Context identity, Journals, Worldline branches, and the presentation inputs needed to reproduce a trace.
Add save/load, deterministic replay, timeline and branch inspection, and comparison of reference evaluation with captured presentation inputs.
Keep snapshots and caches derived and discardable unless a measured requirement promotes one into an explicit contract.
Accept:
The canonical trace round-trips through save/load with identical events, branch identity, evaluated states, and visible presentation inputs.
Unsupported or incompatible versions fail explicitly, and replay can scrub, fork, and reproduce the saved result without hidden frame history.
Any promoted snapshot or cache has an identity, invalidation, and compatibility rule backed by a measured need.
> Gate: Choose the serialization format, schema/version policy, and compatibility guarantees.
> Gate: Decide which snapshots and caches are derived; do not make persistence of presentation history a default.
> Gate: Defer network synchronization and merge semantics until a concrete product requirement activates them.
