[performance] Measurement and performance hardening (notstarted)
-> deterministic-kernel
-> playback-presentation
-> canonical-game-slice
Files:
crates/benchmarks/benches/engine.rs
crates/benchmarks/fixtures/
crates/benchmarks/reports/
Do:
Measure journal length, evaluation cost, scrub latency, branch count, frame production, and animation workload on fixed canonical traces.
Optimize only behind the approved pure contracts, keeping the deterministic evaluator as an oracle and isolating benchmark and cache policy from game rules.
Cross-check every optimized evaluator or presentation path against the reference evaluator and record benchmark conditions, data, and regime limits.
Accept:
The benchmark suite reports reproducible measurements for the target regime and identifies the cost of each accepted optimization.
Optimized and reference outputs agree on deterministic fixtures and representative traces, including state-owned LogicalTime and state-plus-Tau presentation.
No optimization depends on unrecorded previous frames or changes a semantic gate without reopening its owning contract task.
> Gate: Define the target scale, workload, hardware, and latency budget from canonical evidence before selecting optimizations.
> Gate: Decide whether memoization or materialization is lawful and specify identity and invalidation from the approved contracts.
> Gate: Keep final GPU architecture stage-gated; persistent simulation driven by unrecorded frame history is outside the current model.
