[purity-hardening] Compiler-checked purity hardening (notstarted)
-> canonical-game-slice
-> replay-persistence
-> performance
-> productization
Files:
crates/engine-core/
crates/presentation/
crates/purity-tests/
Do:
Narrow the public authoritative and presentation boundaries after the behavior, game slice, proof package, persistence, and performance regime are known.
Use closed DSL values, private constructors, forbidden unsafe code, and compiler-checked negative tests to make prohibited mutation and callback injection ill-typed.
Keep any remaining limitations of admitted code explicit; a lint is supplementary and does not replace the data-only boundary.
Accept:
trybuild or equivalent compiler tests prove that callers cannot obtain mutable authoritative state, assign event timestamps outside the journal writer, inject hidden transition callbacks, or mutate published journals and branches.
The hardened API preserves the conformance results and measured behavior established by earlier stages.
> Gate: Choose the final public crate boundaries and compile-fail test policy after the actual DSL, game, and workload are known.